#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 741.12pt, "*Le Zhao: le.zhao@tuwien.ac.at")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 749.88pt, "†")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(75.24pt, 753.36pt, "Amalio Fern")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.2pt, 753.36pt, "á")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(128.64pt, 753.36pt, "ndez-Pacheco: amalio.fernandez-pacheco@tuwien.ac.at  ")
  #line-at(503.696pt, 753.36pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(105.96pt, 81.36pt, "II. EXPERIMENTAL METHODS ")
  #line-at(119.64pt, 104.28pt, "A. MOKE microscopy setup  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 127.32pt, "A home-built MOKE microscope was employed for ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.84pt, "the experiments. The illumination source was a high-")
  #line-at(72pt, 150.36pt, "power LED with four LED units, configured in a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 161.88pt, "Köhler illumination scheme [26] to ensure uniform ")
  #line-at(72pt, 173.28pt, "sample illumination. Two Glan-Taylor polarizers ")
  #line-at(72pt, 184.8pt, "served as the polarizer and analyzer, respectively, and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 196.32pt, "a λ/4 waveplate was used as the compensator. Imaging ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.84pt, "was performed using a 20×/0.5 objective and a digital ")
  #line-at(72pt, 219.36pt, "CMOS camera. A piezo stage with ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.12pt, 219.36pt, "z")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(222.96pt, 219.36pt, "-axis movement ")
  #line-at(72pt, 230.88pt, "was implemented for focusing and adjusting the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 242.28pt, "distance between the sample surface and the objective, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 253.8pt, "as illustrated in Fig. 1(a). A three-dimensional ")
  #line-at(72pt, 265.32pt, "magnetic field was generated by a hexapole ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.84pt, "electromagnet, with its strength and orientation ")
  #line-at(72pt, 288.36pt, "monitored using an ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(155.28pt, 288.36pt, "in-situ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(180.72pt, 288.36pt, " 3D magnetic field sensor ")
  #line-at(72pt, 299.88pt, "and three unidirectional Hall sensors mounted on the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 311.28pt, "pole pieces of the electromagnet [27]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(94.08pt, 334.32pt, "B. Workflow for EDOF MOKE imaging  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 357.36pt, "In our EDOF MOKE imaging scenario, a through-")
  #line-at(72pt, 368.76pt, "focus-scanning-based approach was adopted, with the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 380.28pt, "overall workflow illustrated in Fig. 1(b) (see also ")
  #line-at(72pt, 391.8pt, "section III.A-C for details). The central idea of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 403.32pt, "through-focus scanning is to capture images at ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.84pt, "different focal planes, so that features located at ")
  #line-at(72pt, 426.36pt, "various sample heights can be clearly resolved and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 437.76pt, "stored in separate frames. A subsequent reconstruction ")
  #line-at(72pt, 449.28pt, "step then stitches together the sharp features from each ")
  #line-at(72pt, 460.8pt, "frame to generate an all-in-focus image. When adapted ")
  #line-at(72pt, 472.32pt, "to MOKE imaging, however, this procedure requires ")
  #line-at(72pt, 483.84pt, "specific modifications with respect to background ")
  #line-at(72pt, 495.36pt, "subtraction. In conventional MOKE microscopy, a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 506.76pt, "uniform background image taken at the saturated state ")
  #line-at(72pt, 518.28pt, "of the sample is typically subtracted from the signal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 529.8pt, "image to ensure a good signal-to-noise ratio. For non-")
  #line-at(72pt, 541.32pt, "planar structures, where magnetization information is ")
  #line-at(72pt, 552.84pt, "distributed ")
  #line-at(125.609pt, 552.84pt, "across ")
  #line-at(161.327pt, 552.84pt, "different ")
  #line-at(206.576pt, 552.84pt, "heights, ")
  #line-at(248.774pt, 552.84pt, "a ")
  #line-at(264.022pt, 552.84pt, "single ")
  #line-at(72pt, 564.24pt, "background image is thus insufficient for all focal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 575.76pt, "planes. Instead, a series of background images ")
  #line-at(72pt, 587.28pt, "corresponding to different heights must be captured in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 598.8pt, "advance. These images form a ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(197.04pt, 598.8pt, "Background Stack")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(270.36pt, 598.8pt, " that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 610.32pt, "serves as a reference for image reconstruction. Once ")
  #line-at(72pt, 621.84pt, "the external magnetic field is changed, another series ")
  #line-at(72pt, 633.24pt, "of images within the range of interest is acquired, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 644.76pt, "forming a ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.72pt, 644.76pt, "Signal Stack")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165pt, 644.76pt, " that contains the non-uniform ")
  #line-at(72pt, 656.28pt, "magnetization signals at different heights. After lateral ")
  #line-at(72pt, 667.8pt, "drift compensation and height matching between those ")
  #line-at(72pt, 679.32pt, "two stacks (see section III.A), background subtraction ")
  #line-at(72pt, 690.84pt, "is performed between each background-signal image ")
  #line-at(72pt, 702.24pt, "pair to obtain a ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.36pt, 702.24pt, "Subtracted Stack")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.36pt, 702.24pt, ". The sharpness of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 713.76pt, "each image in the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.84pt, 713.76pt, "Subtracted Stack")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(216.12pt, 713.76pt, " is then evaluated ")
  #line-at(324pt, 81.36pt, "using a Sobel filter (which is generally a derivative of ")
  #line-at(324pt, 92.88pt, "the image), and the final image can be reconstructed ")
  #line-at(324pt, 104.28pt, "by stitching together the sharpest regions (see section ")
  #line-at(324pt, 115.8pt, "III.B). ")
  #line-at(324pt, 138.84pt, "Practically, we tested the EDOF MOKE imaging ")
  #line-at(324pt, 150.36pt, "method on a Ta(5)/Co")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
