  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(446.28pt, 151.32pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(452.76pt, 150.36pt, "(0.8)/MgO(1.1)/Ta(2) ")
  #line-at(324pt, 161.88pt, "multilayer (all thicknesses are in nanometers) showing ")
  #line-at(324pt, 173.28pt, "perpendicular magnetic anisotropy (PMA). The ")
  #line-at(324pt, 184.8pt, "sample was tilted by 10° to mimic a non-planar ")
  #line-at(324pt, 196.32pt, "structure. The range of through-focus scanning was ")
  #line-at(324pt, 207.96pt, "± 24")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(342.12pt, 207.96pt, " μm with a step size of")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(456.72pt, 207.96pt, " 200 nm. We also ")
  #line-at(324pt, 219.6pt, "performed additional post-processing to the stitching ")
  #line-at(324pt, 231pt, "results for further enhancing the signal-to-noise ratio ")
  #line-at(324pt, 242.52pt, "(see section III.C). All those reconstruction products ")
  #line-at(324pt, 254.04pt, "were then evaluated and compared quantitively in ")
  #line-at(324pt, 265.56pt, "section III.D. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(343.44pt, 288.6pt, "III. ALGORITHM DESCRIPTION AND ")
  #line-at(398.04pt, 300pt, "EVALUATION ")
  #line-at(339.48pt, 323.04pt, "A. Drift compensation and height matching ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324pt, 346.08pt, "Drifts in a MOKE microscope induced by the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 357.6pt, "application of magnetic fields, mechanical instabilities ")
  #line-at(324pt, 369pt, "or thermal fluctuations can compromise the image ")
  #line-at(324pt, 380.52pt, "quality, especially after background subtraction. For a ")
  #line-at(324pt, 392.04pt, "through-focus scanning scenario of three-dimensional ")
  #line-at(324pt, 403.56pt, "structures, drifts along the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.2pt, 403.56pt, "z")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(434.04pt, 403.56pt, "-direction may also lead to ")
  #line-at(324pt, 415.08pt, "varying degrees of defocusing across the sample, ")
  #line-at(324pt, 426.48pt, "which cannot be easily corrected only by two-")
  #line-at(324pt, 438pt, "dimensional image alignment. Therefore, matching ")
  #line-at(324pt, 449.52pt, "each signal image to a specific background image ")
  #line-at(324pt, 461.04pt, "taken at exactly the same height together with the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 472.56pt, "lateral drift compensation must be achieved before ")
  #line-at(324pt, 484.08pt, "image reconstruction. In order to enable automated ")
  #line-at(324pt, 495.48pt, "processing, we sequentially applied a Sobel filter and ")
  #line-at(324pt, 507pt, "a Gaussian filter to the signal image (Figs. 2(a-c)). ")
  #line-at(324pt, 518.52pt, "Features used for alignment were then selected from a ")
  #line-at(324pt, 530.04pt, "21×21-pixel square region centered around each ")
  #line-at(324pt, 541.56pt, "global maxima, as shown in Fig. 2(d). These steps help ")
  #line-at(324pt, 553.08pt, "to guarantee that the selected region is always located ")
  #line-at(324pt, 564.48pt, "within the in-focus area. ")
  #line-at(324pt, 587.52pt, "Alignment was performed between the selected signal ")
  #line-at(324pt, 599.04pt, "image and a series of background images with the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 610.68pt, "relative nominal height offset defined as ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(488.88pt, 610.68pt, "Δℎ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(500.52pt, 610.68pt, " (Fig. 2e). ")
  #line-at(324pt, 622.2pt, "An algorithm based on the normalized cross-")
  #line-at(324pt, 633.72pt, "correlation coefficient was utilized using the Fiji ")
  #line-at(324pt, 645.24pt, "software for drift compensation [28,29], with the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 657.12pt, "searching window set to 5 pixels (")
  #line-at(483.086pt, 657.12pt, " ≈")
  #line-at(498.48pt, 657.12pt, " 1.47 μm). ")
  #line-at(324pt, 670.32pt, "Figs. 2(f) and 2(g) show the subtracted images before ")
  #line-at(324pt, 681.84pt, "and after drift compensation, respectively, from which ")
  #line-at(324pt, 693.24pt, "it can be observed that non-magnetic features cannot ")
  #line-at(324pt, 704.76pt, "be eliminated through subtraction if the heights of the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 716.28pt, "signal and background images are not identical. ")
