  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 483.84pt, "To validate the reliability and applicability of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 495.36pt, "EDOF MOKE imaging approach presented here, we ")
  #line-at(72pt, 506.76pt, "conducted experiments on another sample composed ")
  #line-at(72pt, 518.28pt, "of Ta(5)/[Co")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(122.64pt, 519.24pt, "40")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(129.12pt, 518.28pt, "Fe")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(139.08pt, 519.24pt, "40")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.56pt, 518.28pt, "B")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(152.16pt, 519.24pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(158.64pt, 518.28pt, "(0.8)/MgO(1.1)/Ta(1)]")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.36pt, 519.24pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(252.6pt, 518.28pt, "/Ta(1) as ")
  #line-at(72pt, 529.8pt, "a representative case. This sample was prepared near ")
  #line-at(72pt, 541.32pt, "the spin reorientation transition at room temperature ")
  #line-at(72pt, 552.84pt, "and ")
  #line-at(100.63pt, 552.84pt, "exhibits ")
  #line-at(146.33pt, 552.84pt, "a ")
  #line-at(164.919pt, 552.84pt, "perpendicularly ")
  #line-at(242.019pt, 552.84pt, "magnetized ")
  #line-at(72pt, 564.24pt, "labyrinthine domain pattern in the demagnetized state, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 575.76pt, "whose characteristic domain size is determined solely ")
  #line-at(72pt, 587.28pt, "by its intrinsic magnetic parameters [35]. Such a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 598.8pt, "property makes it suitable as a standard specimen for ")
  #line-at(72pt, 610.32pt, "assessing imaging performance under various tilt ")
  #line-at(72pt, 621.84pt, "angles. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 644.76pt, "Using the previously described stitching method (see ")
  #line-at(72pt, 656.28pt, "section III.B.2), the magnetic domain morphologies at ")
  #line-at(72pt, 667.8pt, "different sample tilt angles were reconstructed from ")
  #line-at(72pt, 679.32pt, "acquired raw images, as shown in Fig. 5(a). It should ")
  #line-at(72pt, 690.84pt, "be noted that the illumination cannot be maintained ")
  #line-at(72pt, 702.24pt, "uniformly across the sample")
  #line-at(186.48pt, 702.24pt, "due to the tilted reflective ")
  #line-at(72pt, 713.76pt, "surface, which leads to brightness inhomogeneities in ")
  #line-at(324pt, 81.36pt, "these reconstructed images. To eliminate the influence ")
  #line-at(324pt, 92.88pt, "of this effect on domain pattern characterization, the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 104.28pt, "reconstructed images were then binarized for further ")
  #line-at(324pt, 115.8pt, "analysis (Fig. 5(b)). ")
  #line-at(324pt, 138.84pt, "The domain pattern acquired from a tilted surface ")
  #line-at(324pt, 150.36pt, "represents the projection of the actual domain structure ")
  #line-at(324pt, 161.88pt, "along the tilted surface onto the horizontal plane. In ")
  #line-at(324pt, 173.28pt, "other words, for the inherently isotropic labyrinthine ")
  #line-at(324pt, 184.8pt, "domains, tilting the sample results in the compression ")
  #line-at(324pt, 196.32pt, "of the pattern along the tilt direction by a factor of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324pt, 207.96pt, "cos 𝜃")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(347.16pt, 207.96pt, ". This geometric effect can be quantitatively ")
  #line-at(324pt, 219.6pt, "verified by comparing the domain periodicities along ")
  #line-at(324pt, 231pt, "the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(340.44pt, 231pt, "x")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(344.88pt, 231pt, "- and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(371.16pt, 231pt, "y")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.6pt, 231pt, "-directions. Through")
  #line-at(463.92pt, 231pt, "performing a two-")
  #line-at(324pt, 242.52pt, "dimensional fast Fourier transform (2D FFT) on the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 254.04pt, "binarized images, the intensity distributions in the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 265.56pt, "frequency domain were obtained, as shown in ")
  #line-at(324pt, 277.08pt, "Fig. 5(c). Radial profiles along ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(460.44pt, 277.08pt, "x")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.88pt, 277.08pt, "- and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(492.96pt, 277.08pt, "y")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(497.28pt, 277.08pt, "-directions ")
  #line-at(324pt, 288.6pt, "within a ± 15° range were extracted and averaged, ")
  #line-at(324pt, 300pt, "yielding the directional intensity distributions as a ")
  #line-at(324pt, 311.52pt, "function of spatial frequency, as illustrated in ")
  #line-at(324pt, 323.04pt, "Figs. 5(d-e), respectively. Gaussian fitting was then ")
  #line-at(324pt, 334.56pt, "applied to determine the peak positions, based on ")
  #line-at(324pt, 346.08pt, "which the spatial frequencies at each tilt angle were ")
  #line-at(324pt, 357.6pt, "obtained (see Fig. 5(f)). The horizontal spatial ")
  #line-at(324pt, 369.12pt, "frequency ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(366.48pt, 369.12pt, "𝑓")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(370.08pt, 371.16pt, "௫")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.76pt, 369.12pt, " increases with the tilt angle, whereas the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 380.88pt, "vertical frequency ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(399.48pt, 380.88pt, "𝑓")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.08pt, 382.92pt, "௬")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(408pt, 380.88pt, " remains mostly unchanged. The ")
  #line-at(324pt, 393.84pt, "resulting frequency ratio ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(437.04pt, 393.84pt, "𝑓")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(440.64pt, 395.88pt, "௫")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(450.84pt, 393.84pt, "𝑓")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.44pt, 395.88pt, "௬")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.32pt, 393.48pt, "⁄")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(462.84pt, 393.84pt, " was subsequently ")
  #line-at(324pt, 406.56pt, "calculated and presented in Fig. 5(g), alongside the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 418.2pt, "theoretical expectation of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(444pt, 418.2pt, "1")
  #line-at(455.035pt, 418.2pt, "cos 𝜃")
  #line-at(449.52pt, 417.84pt, "⁄")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.2pt, 418.2pt, ". Within the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 429.72pt, "experimental uncertainty, the measured frequency ")
  #line-at(324pt, 441.24pt, "ratio agrees well with the theoretical prediction, ")
  #line-at(324pt, 452.76pt, "further confirming the validity of the image-stitching ")
  #line-at(324pt, 464.28pt, "procedure and demonstrating its applicability to ")
  #line-at(324pt, 475.8pt, "magnetic imaging on non-planar surfaces. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(340.08pt, 498.72pt, "B. Kerr response to in-plane magnetization ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(324pt, 521.76pt, "In addition to the domain image reconstruction of ")
  #line-at(324pt, 533.28pt, "PMA samples, the capability of imaging in-plane (IP) ")
  #line-at(324pt, 544.8pt, "magnetization, as well as to investigate quantitatively ")
  #line-at(324pt, 556.2pt, "the response to non-planar IP components, constitutes ")
  #line-at(324pt, 567.72pt, "another ")
  #line-at(366.465pt, 567.72pt, "important ")
  #line-at(417.558pt, 567.72pt, "aspect ")
  #line-at(454.867pt, 567.72pt, "for ")
  #line-at(478.855pt, 567.72pt, "3D ")
  #line-at(503.409pt, 567.72pt, "magnetic ")
  #line-at(324pt, 579.24pt, "imaging [36]. For this purpose, we employed a 40-nm-")
  #line-at(324pt, 590.76pt, "thick CoFeB film as a representative IP sample. In ")
  #line-at(324pt, 602.28pt, "conventional MOKE microscopy, illumination and ")
  #line-at(324pt, 613.8pt, "collection optical paths are usually perpendicular to ")
  #line-at(324pt, 625.2pt, "the sample surface, and the detection of in-plane ")
  #line-at(324pt, 636.72pt, "magnetization signals is made possible by selecting ")
  #line-at(324pt, 648.24pt, "specific wave vectors of the incident light. However, ")
  #line-at(324pt, 659.76pt, "for a tilted sample surface, the effective incident angle ")
  #line-at(324pt, 671.28pt, "differs from that in the untilted configuration, giving ")
  #line-at(324pt, 682.8pt, "rise to additional contributions to the detection ")
  #line-at(324pt, 694.2pt, "sensitivity of in-plane magnetization [37,38]. The ")
  #line-at(324pt, 705.72pt, "corresponding ")
  #line-at(391.876pt, 705.72pt, "signal ")
  #line-at(426.242pt, 705.72pt, "response ")
  #line-at(471.634pt, 705.72pt, "and ")
  #line-at(496.586pt, 705.72pt, "underlying ")
  #line-at(324pt, 717.24pt, "mechanisms are discussed in detail below. ")
]

