  #line-at(72pt, 92.88pt, "In our measurement system, the wave vector selection ")
  #line-at(72pt, 104.28pt, "was implemented by inserting a rotatable aperture with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 115.8pt, "one off-axis hole at the conjugate position of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 127.32pt, "objective’s back focal plane. This configuration allows ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.84pt, "only the light passing through the hole to reach the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 150.36pt, "sample surface, while blocking all the other ")
  #line-at(72pt, 161.88pt, "components. The first column of Fig. 6(a) shows the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 173.28pt, "images at the back focal plane of the objective during ")
  #line-at(72pt, 184.8pt, "the measurement of a planar sample, after inserting an ")
  #line-at(72pt, 196.32pt, "auxiliary Bertrand lens in the optical path before the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.84pt, "tube lens and camera. Since those images are reflected ")
  #line-at(72pt, 219.36pt, "once from the sample surface before being collected ")
  #line-at(72pt, 230.88pt, "by the detector, they appear horizontally flipped. Here ")
  #line-at(72pt, 242.28pt, "the image edges are defined by the size of objective’s ")
  #line-at(72pt, 253.8pt, "back pupil, as indicated by the yellow circles. As the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 265.32pt, "sample’s tilt angle increases, the LED images can be ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.84pt, "seen moving progressively to the right with respect to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 288.36pt, "the front pupil indicated by the white circles, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 299.88pt, "eventually moving beyond its boundary. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 322.8pt, "The corresponding hysteresis loops under each ")
  #line-at(72pt, 334.32pt, "illumination and tilting condition are presented in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 345.84pt, "Figs. 6(b-d), respectively. Note that the applied ")
  #line-at(72pt, 357.36pt, "magnetic field was always aligned with the tilted ")
  #line-at(72pt, 368.76pt, "sample plane by means of the hexapole electromagnet ")
  #line-at(72pt, 380.28pt, "available in our setup [27]. Under the top-LED ")
  #line-at(72pt, 391.8pt, "illumination, the absolute switching amplitude of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 403.32pt, "hysteresis loop exhibits a monotonic decrease with the ")
