#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 741.12pt, "*Le Zhao: le.zhao@tuwien.ac.at")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 749.88pt, "†")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(75.24pt, 753.36pt, "Amalio Fern")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.2pt, 753.36pt, "á")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(128.64pt, 753.36pt, "ndez-Pacheco: amalio.fernandez-pacheco@tuwien.ac.at  ")
  #line-at(503.696pt, 753.36pt, "9 ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 92.88pt, "Returning to the response under all-LED illumination, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 104.28pt, "since the overall illumination changes moderately ")
  #line-at(72pt, 115.8pt, "from 0° to 5°, the Kerr response at a tilt angle of 5° is ")
  #line-at(72pt, 127.32pt, "primarily governed by the changes in the effective ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.84pt, "incident angle, which has the same sign as that of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 150.36pt, "bottom-LED illumination. For tilt angles larger than ")
  #line-at(72pt, 161.88pt, "10°, the absence of reflected light from the bottom-")
  #line-at(72pt, 173.28pt, "LED unit induces the dominance of top-LED unit, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 184.8pt, "thereby reversing the overall measured switching ")
  #line-at(72pt, 196.32pt, "direction. Owing to the competing contributions from ")
  #line-at(72pt, 207.84pt, "the top- and bottom-LED illuminations, the Kerr ")
  #line-at(72pt, 219.36pt, "response under all-LED illumination always lies ")
  #line-at(72pt, 230.88pt, "between those obtained under the two individual ")
  #line-at(72pt, 242.28pt, "illumination conditions, as revealed in Fig. 6(f). It is ")
  #line-at(72pt, 253.8pt, "worth noting that although only the Köhler ")
  #line-at(72pt, 265.32pt, "illumination path is depicted here, these arguments can ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.84pt, "be generalized to other configurations as the effective ")
  #line-at(72pt, 288.36pt, "collecting angle of the objective remains unchanged. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 311.28pt, "The analysis above reveals the capability of detecting ")
  #line-at(72pt, 322.8pt, "in-plane magnetized signals from a non-planar sample ")
  #line-at(72pt, 334.32pt, "surface. Even under all-LED illumination without ")
  #line-at(72pt, 345.84pt, "additional wave vectors selections, the MOKE ")
  #line-at(72pt, 357.36pt, "microscope retains an intrinsic sensitivity to the in-")
  #line-at(72pt, 368.76pt, "plane magnetization along the tilting direction, as long ")
  #line-at(72pt, 380.4pt, "as the tilting angle is smaller than ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(208.08pt, 380.4pt, "arcsin(NA)")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.48pt, 380.4pt, " defined ")
  #line-at(72pt, 392.04pt, "by the objective. Building on this intrinsic sensitivity, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 403.56pt, "we performed imaging of the in-plane magnetized ")
  #line-at(72pt, 415.08pt, "domains under all-LED illumination, with the tilt ")
  #line-at(72pt, 426.48pt, "angle set at 10° to maximize the magneto-optical Kerr ")
  #line-at(72pt, 438pt, "response. The directly imaged domain pattern is ")
  #line-at(72pt, 449.52pt, "shown in Fig. 7(e). Sharpness analysis (Fig. 7(f)) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 461.04pt, "indicates that the domain boundaries are well defined ")
  #line-at(72pt, 472.56pt, "near the center but blurred towards the edges. By ")
  #line-at(72pt, 484.08pt, "employing the previously described through-focus ")
  #line-at(72pt, 495.48pt, "scanning followed by image-stitching procedures (see ")
  #line-at(72pt, 507pt, "section III.B.2), we obtained the reconstructed image ")
  #line-at(72pt, 518.52pt, "shown in Fig. 7(g), which is well-resolved and clear ")
  #line-at(72pt, 530.04pt, "across the entire field of view, with a 38% ")
  #line-at(72pt, 541.56pt, "improvement in edge sharpness indicated in Fig. 7(h). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.16pt, 564.48pt, "V. CONCLUSIONS ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 587.52pt, "In summary, we have presented an extended depth of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 599.04pt, "field MOKE microscopy approach capable of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 610.56pt, "capturing high-quality magnetic domain images on ")
  #line-at(72pt, 621.96pt, "non-planar sample surfaces. By performing through-")
  #line-at(72pt, 633.48pt, "focus scanning followed by image-stitching based on ")
  #line-at(72pt, 645pt, "sharpness analysis, we obtain magnetic domain ")
  #line-at(72pt, 656.52pt, "images that are both sharp and well-resolved across ")
  #line-at(72pt, 668.04pt, "the entire field of view. While the Real-Shape-Guided ")
  #line-at(72pt, 679.56pt, "Stitching method proves effective in preserving edge ")
  #line-at(72pt, 690.96pt, "sharpness and suppressing random noise, PSF-based ")
  #line-at(72pt, 702.48pt, "reconstruction methods can further enhance both the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 714pt, "signal-to-noise ratio and edge definition, particularly ")
  #line-at(324pt, 81.36pt, "in regions affected by high-frequency noise or imaging ")
  #line-at(324pt, 92.88pt, "defects. The reliability of such reconstruction strategy ")
  #line-at(324pt, 104.28pt, "is quantitatively assessed by measuring and stitching ")
  #line-at(324pt, 115.8pt, "domain images of a perpendicularly magnetized ")
  #line-at(324pt, 127.32pt, "sample ")
  #line-at(362.956pt, 127.32pt, "exhibiting ")
  #line-at(414.287pt, 127.32pt, "isotropic ")
  #line-at(459.865pt, 127.32pt, "periodic ")
  #line-at(503.363pt, 127.32pt, "magnetic ")
  #line-at(324pt, 138.84pt, "domains in the demagnetized state at different tilt ")
  #line-at(324pt, 150.36pt, "angles. The observed spatial frequency of domains ")
  #line-at(324pt, 161.88pt, "extracted from FFT analysis follows the expected ")
  #line-at(324pt, 173.28pt, "1/cos")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(345.12pt, 173.28pt, "θ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(350.04pt, 173.28pt, " dependence on the tilt angle. The measurement ")
  #line-at(324pt, 184.8pt, "response for an in-plane magnetized sample is also ")
  #line-at(324pt, 196.32pt, "systematically investigated by varying the tilt angle ")
  #line-at(324pt, 207.84pt, "under different illumination schemes. After analyzing ")
  #line-at(324pt, 219.36pt, "the contributions of individual wave vectors from each ")
  #line-at(324pt, 230.88pt, "LED unit, we have quantified how the effective ")
  #line-at(324pt, 242.28pt, "incident angles influence the MOKE signal for in-")
  #line-at(324pt, 253.8pt, "plane magnetization, demonstrating quantitively the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 265.32pt, "intrinsic capability of MOKE microscopy to resolve ")
  #line-at(324pt, 276.84pt, "in-plane magnetic signals on non-planar surfaces. ")
  #line-at(324pt, 299.88pt, "Although demonstrated here as proof-of-concept cases ")
  #line-at(324pt, 311.28pt, "with intentionally tilted flat samples, the presented ")
  #line-at(324pt, 322.8pt, "methods and findings can be readily extended to more ")
  #line-at(324pt, 334.32pt, "complicated 3D geometries. Compared to X-ray-based ")
  #line-at(324pt, 345.84pt, "magnetic domain reconstruction techniques, the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 357.36pt, "simplicity and flexibility of this laboratory-accessible ")
  #line-at(324pt, 368.76pt, "method allow it to be easily implemented in standard ")
  #line-at(324pt, 380.28pt, "MOKE microscopy setups with only moderate ")
  #line-at(324pt, 391.8pt, "modifications, extending its availability to a wide ")
  #line-at(324pt, 403.32pt, "research community. Due to its relatively fast imaging ")
  #line-at(324pt, 414.84pt, "speeds, it can also facilitate real-time observations of ")
  #line-at(324pt, 426.36pt, "magnetic domain evolution and dynamics. ")
  #line-at(324pt, 449.28pt, "Additionally, it is worth noting that light reflected ")
  #line-at(324pt, 460.8pt, "from off-focus surface regions may interfere with the ")
  #line-at(324pt, 472.32pt, "reconstruction process. An effective solution in that ")
  #line-at(324pt, 483.84pt, "case, inspired by the widely used confocal microscopy ")
  #line-at(324pt, 495.36pt, "technique in biological research [39], could comprise ")
  #line-at(324pt, 506.76pt, "inserting a pinhole together with auxiliary lenses into ")
  #line-at(324pt, 518.28pt, "the imaging path before the camera [40]. This ")
  #line-at(324pt, 529.8pt, "configuration selectively collects signals originating ")
  #line-at(324pt, 541.32pt, "only from the focal plane, which are subsequently used ")
  #line-at(324pt, 552.84pt, "for image reconstruction. There are also additional ")
  #line-at(324pt, 564.24pt, "algorithms for reconstruction involving neural ")
  #line-at(324pt, 575.76pt, "networks and deep learning [41], but these are beyond ")
  #line-at(324pt, 587.28pt, "the scope of the present manuscript. Future ")
  #line-at(324pt, 598.8pt, "improvements could also involve synchronization ")
  #line-at(324pt, 610.32pt, "with pulsed magnetic fields or the implementation of ")
  #line-at(324pt, 621.84pt, "real-time image processing, to enable the time-")
  #line-at(324pt, 633.24pt, "resolved measurement of magnetization dynamics. ")
  #line-at(324pt, 644.76pt, "We believe that the continued development of such ")
  #line-at(324pt, 656.28pt, "integrated imaging strategies promises to provide a ")
  #line-at(324pt, 667.8pt, "powerful tool for investigating surface magnetization ")
  #line-at(324pt, 679.32pt, "states in 3D geometries, thereby opening new avenues ")
  #line-at(324pt, 690.84pt, "for ")
  #line-at(347.063pt, 690.84pt, "tabletop ")
  #line-at(390.324pt, 690.84pt, "studies ")
  #line-at(429.301pt, 690.84pt, "of ")
  #line-at(448.885pt, 690.84pt, "non-planar ")
  #line-at(503.379pt, 690.84pt, "magnetic ")
  #line-at(324pt, 702.24pt, "nanostructures and spintronic devices. ")
]

